data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":659,"output_index":1,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0732eb379f8a4c18016aca937eefa88193a3292b06961f8b8d","call_id":"call_29e155d252de43ce93362ff3d9fd2042","name":"edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"server.js\",\"edits\":[{\"oldText\":\"CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS projects (id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, created_at INTEGER NOT NULL);\",\"newText\":\"CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS projects (id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, created_at INTEGER NOT NULL, archived INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0);\"},{\"oldText\":\"const insertProject = db.prepare('INSERT INTO projects (id, name, created_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?)');\\nconst listProjects = db.prepare('SELECT id, name FROM projects ORDER BY created_at, rowid');\\nconst findProject = db.prepare('SELECT id, name FROM projects WHERE id = ?');\",\"newText\":\"try { db.exec('ALTER TABLE projects ADD COLUMN archived INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0'); } catch {}\\nconst insertProject = db.prepare('INSERT INTO projects (id, name, created_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?)');\\nconst listProjects = db.prepare(`SELECT p.id, p.name, p.archived, COUNT(t.id) AS total_count, COALESCE(SUM(t.completed), 0) AS completed_count FROM projects p LEFT JOIN tasks t ON t.project_id = p.id GROUP BY p.id ORDER BY p.created_at, p.rowid`);\\nconst findProject = db.prepare('SELECT id, name, archived FROM projects WHERE id = ?');\\nconst setArchived = db.prepare('UPDATE projects SET archived = ? WHERE id = ?');\"},{\"oldText\":\"if (req.method === 'GET' && url.pathname === '/api/projects') return send(200, JSON.stringify(listProjects.all()));\",\"newText\":\"if (req.method === 'GET' && url.pathname === '/api/projects') return send(200, JSON.stringify(listProjects.all()));\\n  const archiveMatch = url.pathname.match(/^\\\\/api\\\\/projects\\\\/([^/]+)\\\\/(archive|restore)$/);\\n  if (req.method === 'POST' && archiveMatch) {\\n    const project = findProject.get(decodeURIComponent(archiveMatch[1]));\\n    if (!project) return send(404, JSON.stringify({ error: 'Project not found' }));\\n    setArchived.run(archiveMatch[2] === 'archive' ? 1 : 0, project.id);\\n    return send(200, JSON.stringify({ ok: true }));\\n  }\"},{\"oldText\":\"if (req.method === 'POST' && !taskMatch[2]) {\\n      try {\",\"newText\":\"if (req.method === 'POST' && !taskMatch[2]) {\\n      if (findProject.get(projectId).archived) return send(409, JSON.stringify({ error: 'Archived project' }));\\n      try {\"},{\"oldText\":\"if (req.method === 'PATCH' && taskMatch[2]) {\\n      try {\",\"newText\":\"if (req.method === 'PATCH' && taskMatch[2]) {\\n      if (findProject.get(projectId).archived) return send(409, JSON.stringify({ error: 'Archived project' }));\\n      try {\"}]}","status":"completed"}}

event: response.completed
data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":660,"response":{"id":"resp_0732eb379f8a4c18016aca937cc4708193a7a232520242033b","object":"response","created_at":1791660924,"completed_at":1791660929,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6-luna","access_programs":null,"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You are an expert coding assistant operating inside pi, a coding agent harness. You help users by reading files, executing commands, editing code, and writing new files.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nIn addition to the tools above, you may have access to other custom tools depending on the project.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for precise changes (edits[].oldText must match exactly)\n- When changing multiple separate locations in one file, use one edit call with multiple entries in edits[] instead of multiple edit calls\n- Each edits[].oldText is matched against the original file, not after earlier edits are applied. Do not emit overlapping or nested edits. Merge nearby changes into one edit.\n- Keep edits[].oldText as small as possible while still being unique in the file. Do not pad with large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about pi itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), pi packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- When working on pi topics, read the docs and examples, and follow .md cross-references before implementing\n- Always read pi .md files completely and follow links to related docs (e.g., tui.md for TUI API details)\n</docs>\n\n<cwd>\n/home/agent/work\n</cwd>","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_0732eb379f8a4c18016aca937d3a3c81939893135907b2829b","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Implementing archive DB migration**"}],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqypN-hqrBRzc-lPHO_7lhYUnwpCO3Aa3cW4GdRUtSETbtjKfzyLUPlYKFX6JPocMf1LdevTw5NzH4q7k6MGlww5f8hIOCPz69jWncjAJjKplE-hkyKFDmg_2pi-5QAqLpWgbeKKIyy9LvI8G4K06m6UmKCNPyZjmbEbZejiOxcJZPO4gq-jDcagWAGvqqEVzImpfxCQlDVMk8lIDTEpTQre0TuPVpVDJNbQ0ng16xt8zxeYbBcURSkZBKbhOgEbFn6yTLaIcimxZs_pODS2qiHdQoedfVMkwg0p38rI5IZdvI579_QUGDQLeAgrjkk3_6mbEfVCjZbeTryhRbm8x7LO8moGmuGcag6wHXGW9wKm0oIUeLAI0qc2JBjtiB9Ta9QxVa8p4DFE71RxItwg5xY3uV-CCH171Fh6UFxnxcWHXC-FAGnKm6A8KPU-w15i-5LmH-4xC9BCdeh2bWyHFDHBjG7G1iBu1DtF8qUjElGWRVOZ_KaTGDTKAMGMtORj1Q6oyzf-vy56db0SUSiX_qeNNKoYjoWSIpM3FebAEf4dydcFgR7amSgbBpFsn2LJwpqu9d2t7YdsTriYmGPdfZ